  "explanation": {
    "contradiction_resolved": "The 793 ms figure represents the raw API network round-trip time for a single completion call on a fast model with an empty rate-limiter queue. In contrast, the 18-35 s per candidate measured in the end-to-end pipeline represents the multi-agent sequence: Explainer agent + Question Generator + Email Drafter + multi-turn Critic and Refinement loop (up to 2 rewrites) under free-tier token-bucket throttling (30 RPM, 7,000 TPM limit) where calls queue for 2-5 seconds between steps. Reasoning models also generate hundreds of chain-of-thought tokens before returning the JSON payload, multiplying the time-to-first-token and overall latency.",
    "production_recommendation": "Use deterministic template generation immediately in the request-response loop (0 ms LLM wait, guaranteed safe). Queue LLM generation asynchronously for FastTrack and Review candidates only using llama-3.1-8b-instant or llama-3.3-70b-versatile, capping daily tokens at 50,000 to prevent quota starvation."
  }
